// `field_specs_of::<T>()` / `construct::<T>(…)` on a type imported from another namespace: the
// turbofish is written with the LOCAL name the `use` binds (`Todo`), and must resolve to the
// declaring module's qualified identity (`app.storage.Todo`) — the key the reflection registry
// actually holds.
//
// The sibling-module case is the sharper one: the entry has no namespace of its own to blame, so
// nothing but the linker's import map can supply the qualification. The parser used to flatten the
// turbofish to the string `"Todo"` before that map was ever consulted, which made both queries
// silently answer as if the type had no fields.
// expect: stdout "id: Type.Int"
// expect: stdout "title: Type.String"
// expect: stdout "built: Todo {id: 1, title: \"a\"}"
// expect: exit 0
use app.storage.Todo;

for spec in field_specs_of::<Todo>() {
    echo "${spec.name}: ${spec.type}";
}

fields: Map<string, dyn> = {"id": 1, "title": "a"};
built = match construct::<Todo>(fields) {
    Ok(v) => "built: ${v}",
    Err(e) => "failed: ${e}",
};
echo built;
